        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: તપવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તપવું — tapvũ — \"to blaze, to be hot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બપોરે સૂરજ તપશે. — bapore sūraj tapśe — \"The sun will blaze at midday.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તપવું (tapvũ) is usually traced to Sanskrit tapyati, \"is hot\". CDIAL does not list tapvũ itself, but it lists the related Gujarati tāpvũ, \"to warm oneself\", under the same entry (CDIAL 5684)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
