          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઉકળાટ — ukaḷāṭ — \"sultry heat, mugginess\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બપોરે ઘણો ઉકળાટ હશે. — bapore ghaṇo ukaḷāṭ haśe — \"It will be very muggy at midday.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઉકળાટ (ukaḷāṭ) is built on the verb ukaḷvũ, \"to boil\", so muggy air is air that seems to boil. CDIAL derives ukaḷvũ from utkalati, \"goes out or up\", a reconstructed form (CDIAL 1716)."
            }
          ]
        },
